 ## Background
-The GPU-Driven Architecture was introduced in the context of scalable web-based volume rendering of large biomedicinal datasets [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the multi-channel page-table hierarchy and residency octree concepts [S1, unofficial]. The approach is similar to previous methods that limit cache misses to manage data transfer [S1, unofficial].
+The GPU-Driven Architecture was introduced in the context of scalable web-based volume rendering of large biomedicinal datasets [S1, unofficial]. It is part of a multi-channel page-table hierarchy system where the residency octree forms the base [S1, unofficial]. The approach extends algorithms from previous work to support multiple channels [S1, unofficial].
 
